<title>USA: XOMA Corp Q4 loss widens.</title>
<headline>XOMA Corp Q4 loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>BERKELEY, Calif. 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>XOMA CORPORATION</p>
<p>		     (in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>				     Three Months	Twelve Months</p>
<p>					   Ended		  Ended</p>
<p>					December 31	 December 31</p>
<p>				     1996	1995     1996	1995</p>
<p>Revenues:			 7,795    5,752    31,826    27,469</p>
<p>Other Income (Expense):</p>
<p>  Investment income	     600	411     2,011     1,934</p>
<p>  Interest expense and other    1	(22)     (399)    1,898</p>
<p>Net Loss		     $(9,669) $(5,332) $(29,110) $(22,472)</p>
<p>Net Loss per Common Share $(0.27)  $(0.22)   $(0.90)   $(0.95)</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p> shares outstanding	  36,101   24,268    32,493    23,671</p>
<p>NOTE: XOMA's net loss for the year ending December 31, 1996 included a $2.5 million provision for costs of settling a class action lawsuit.</p>
<p>1995 income included a one-time net gain of $1.9 million related to restructuring of the company's E5(R) agreement with Pfizer Inc and certain other matters.</p>
